<%# Involuntary-churn recovery. When a subscription charge fails, Stripe
    retries it for ~3 weeks (past_due) before giving up (unpaid -> canceled).
    Through that whole window the organization has already lost its
    Compliance Packet allowance and DSCSA verification badge, but nothing
    tells them why unless they happen to open the Billing page. This banner
    rides every authenticated page with a one-click path to the Stripe
    portal to fix the card -- the single highest-leverage retention prompt
    for a subscription business. %>
<% if current_subscription&.payment_failing? %>
  <div class="px-7 pt-4">
    <div class="rounded border border-[#f0c8c2] bg-[#fdeceb] text-[#b42318] px-4 py-3 text-sm flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <span>
        <span class="font-semibold">Your last payment didn't go through.</span>
        Update your card to keep GPS tracking, Compliance Packets, and your DSCSA verification badge active.
      </span>
      <%= button_to "Update payment method", billing_portal_path, method: :post,
            class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap" %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
